;; What the model reads of each tool brainyard/share_tools.clj defines: its description,
;; by tool id (brainyard.tool-words, byj-2e8.5). Read by the model, so a
;; resource (RFC-001).
{"share$status"
  "Where sharing stands: whether this session is shared, its page, who is watching and in what role, and the other shares this session started."
 "share$ls"
  "What can be shared, from byj-share: this project's byj, Claude Code and Codex sessions, tmux terminals and byj's agents, each with the reference share$start takes (byj:ID, claude:ID, codex:ID, term:NAME, agent:NAME)."
 "share$start"
  "Share this session, or the sessions named, with the people the person invites: they watch it live in a browser. With no :refs, this session. :refs names others — byj:ID, claude:ID, codex:ID (an id prefix will do), term:NAME (a tmux session, made if there is none, typed into from the page), agent:NAME (one of byj's agents — prefer a read-only one such as explore; one that does more than read is shared only once the person confirms it — asked by invited callers), or team; several are shared as one group. Each ends when this session does. Returns the share's page and its coach and watch links once the relay has it open. Publishes what it shares: never start a share the person did not ask for."
 "share$login"
  "Log byj-share in to the relay this session shares through, when share$start says this device is not logged in, or is logged in to another relay. Returns at once with a link and a code the person approves in a browser, and the task that completes once they have; logging in replaces byj-share's login for any other relay."
 "share$record"
  "Turn a running share's recording on or off: this session's (no :ref) or another by reference (byj:ID, claude:ID, term:NAME, agent:NAME …). On, it keeps the share's events from its start and its screen from now, tells everyone watching, and uploads it for review when the share ends; off, it keeps nothing more. Only when the person asked to record, or to stop recording."
 "share$control"
  "Stop, pause or resume a share, or remove someone from this session's. With no :ref, this session's share; with one, that share (byj:ID, claude:ID, term:NAME, agent:NAME …). :user is whom kick removes — share$status names them."
 ;; arguments, as "<tool> :arg", and result fields, as "<tool> result :field" (byj-2e8.9)
 "share$ls :all"
  "Every session on this machine, not only this project's."
 "share$start :refs"
  "What to share; none: this session."
 "share$start :target"
  "link (the default: invite links), or class:CODE to share into a class."
 "share$start :record"
  "Keep it for review when it ends; everyone watching is told."
 "share$start :no-input"
  "A terminal: view-only, nobody types from the page."
 "share$start :chat"
  "A terminal: spectators may chat too (default true)."
 "share$start :max-messages"
  "An agent: how many messages callers may send in all (default 200)."
 "share$start :max-cost"
  "An agent: how much callers' messages may cost in USD (default 10)."
 "share$record :on"
  "true to record, false to stop recording."
 "share$record :ref"
  "Another share; none: this session's."
 "share$control :action"
  "What to do."
 "share$control :ref"
  "Another share to act on; none: this session's."
 "share$control :user"
  "For kick: who to remove."
 ;; what its tools say back to the model, as "<namespace>/<definition>" (byj-2e8.9)
 "share-tools/login"
  "Give the person the link and the code above, word for word, to approve in a browser where they are signed in. Then task$wait on {task-id} (up to 300000 ms): it completes once they approve."
 "share-tools/confirm-agents"
  "not sharing agent:{nm}: it can do more than read, and no one is here to confirm it"
 "share-tools/record!"
  "recording this share — everyone watching is told, and it is uploaded for review when the share ends"
 "share-tools/record! 2"
  "recording stopped — what was kept is uploaded for review when the share ends"
 "share-tools/ls"
  "byj-share is not on PATH — install it (`byj doctor` says how), or set :share-sidecar"}
